 ### [Focus Point Based Brick LOD Selection](5282-focus-point-based-brick-lod-selection.md)
-Focus Point Based Brick LOD Selection is a method to determine the appropriate level-of-detail (LOD) for each brick in a multiscale volume representation based on the distance of the brick's center to a user-defined focus point. It differs from error-driven siblings like [Hierarchical Culling & Multi-resolution Approximation](2010-hierarchical-culling-multi-resolution-approximation.md) because it relies exclusively on geometric proximity to the focus point, ignoring approximation error. This allows for arbitrary texture resolutions per brick, unlike methods with strict texture-to-geometry correspondence. See [Focus Point Based Brick LOD Selection](5282-focus-point-based-brick-lod-selection.md).
