 ### [Face Subsampling](6025-face-subsampling.md)
-Face Subsampling is a Level-of-Detail (LOD) technique for tetrahedral volume rendering that dynamically selects a subset of mesh faces to render, balancing visual fidelity against frame rate constraints. It solves the problem of interactive rendering on large tetrahedral meshes by reducing the number of rasterized primitives without pre-aggregating data into voxels or bricks. It differs from sibling methods like [Hierarchical Culling & Multi-resolution Approximation](2010-hierarchical-culling-multi-resolution-approximation.md) by operating directly on the unstructured mesh topology rather than a hierarchical grid, and from [Focus Point Based Brick LOD Selection](5282-focus-point-based-brick-lod-selection.md) by being primarily face-centric rather than brick-centric. See [Face Subsampling](6025-face-subsampling.md).
